<li>Anna Nalick's song "Sort of Delilah" from the album Broken Dolls &amp; Odds &amp; Ends is written from a guilty and regretful woman's perspective, as evidenced by the lyrics "Heaven was a lot to lose / I just covered your eyes and let you crumble down... / I can't lie love / I'm sort of Delilah / ...I let you down".</li>
